WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.353
- I would say a bond between
the inmate and the horse

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:10.922
is one of the most important
things that they learn.

00:00:10.922 --> 00:00:14.397
When they actually start
to bond with that horse,

00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:16.659
they will become better
trainers, they will become

00:00:16.659 --> 00:00:18.585
better people.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.138
I think that's good that
they feel that much pride

00:00:21.138 --> 00:00:22.728
in their horses.

00:00:22.728 --> 00:00:25.883
It's good to have pride in
something, especially in prison.

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:29.050
(contemplative music)

00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:34.882
(birds chattering)

00:00:34.882 --> 00:00:39.049
Go right up behind his ears
a little bit with that rope.

00:00:40.104 --> 00:00:43.521
Now when that gets up there, he may jump, so.

00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:46.221
Done pretty good.

00:00:47.456 --> 00:00:48.802
My name's Hank Curry.

00:00:48.802 --> 00:00:51.415
I'm the head horse trainer
here at the Northern Nevada

00:00:51.415 --> 00:00:53.546
Correctional Center.

00:00:53.546 --> 00:00:57.514
I've been here 15 years now,
and I'm in charge of about

00:00:57.514 --> 00:00:58.931
20 to 25 inmates.

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.291
We're taking a completely
wild horse and trying

00:01:03.291 --> 00:01:06.809
to domesticate them, get
them where they're a gentle,

00:01:06.809 --> 00:01:07.892
usable horse.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.277
The inmates put in applications
to come to work out here.

00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:17.227
According to their behavior in
prison, we review all of that

00:01:17.227 --> 00:01:20.163
and try to decide whether
or not they could possibly

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.996
become horse trainers.

00:01:24.088 --> 00:01:27.227
To start out with, we
take a totally wild horse,

00:01:27.227 --> 00:01:31.394
and I have my guys actually
put them in a round corral.

00:01:32.739 --> 00:01:34.915
We don't allow them to
rope them or anything else.

00:01:34.915 --> 00:01:38.803
They have to actually make
contact with their hands.

00:01:38.803 --> 00:01:40.826
Most of the inmates have
maybe ridden a horse

00:01:40.826 --> 00:01:43.645
once or twice in their
life, so it takes a lot

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:47.395
of guts, and it takes
a lot of determination.

00:01:49.652 --> 00:01:51.695
- This guy right here didn't
want nothin' to do with me

00:01:51.695 --> 00:01:54.880
and now he's my little
buddy and he follows me

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.213
everywhere I go.

00:01:58.262 --> 00:01:59.941
- It's just a moment
where you bond, you know,

00:01:59.941 --> 00:02:03.156
and you become like best friends.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.819
This guy only did it
within the last few weeks.

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:07.392
It's pretty amazing.

00:02:07.392 --> 00:02:10.544
I mean, I'm not doing time
until I go back to camp.

00:02:10.544 --> 00:02:13.819
You know, and that's when the clock
starts for me as far as

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:14.754
realizing where I'm at.

00:02:14.754 --> 00:02:17.004
When I'm out here I'm free.

00:02:18.929 --> 00:02:21.269
- [Hank] In the last few
years, we've developed

00:02:21.269 --> 00:02:24.637
a lot of horses that have
been used by the Fish and Game

00:02:24.637 --> 00:02:27.298
wardens, the Forestry Service.

00:02:27.298 --> 00:02:31.104
The Sheriff's Department
actually has a mounted group

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:34.691
and those were horses
trained by this program.

00:02:34.691 --> 00:02:38.566
I think that, you know, this job is
kind of inspirational.

00:02:38.566 --> 00:02:41.030
It's not like regular prison
where everybody's running

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.359
around being foul-mouthed,
you know, being a tough guy

00:02:44.359 --> 00:02:45.337
and everything else.

00:02:45.337 --> 00:02:46.932
Doesn't work out here.

00:02:46.932 --> 00:02:49.372
Horses don't care who you
are, how big or how tough

00:02:49.372 --> 00:02:52.549
you are; they will
equalize the playing field

00:02:52.549 --> 00:02:54.962
if you want to play tough.

00:02:54.962 --> 00:02:58.073
I see a great deal of
change in all these guys.

00:02:58.073 --> 00:02:59.667
They seem to mature.

00:02:59.667 --> 00:03:01.460
They're functioning;
they know how to work;

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.134
they know how to hold a job.

00:03:03.134 --> 00:03:06.051
So often it's changed their lives.

